  "items": [
    {
      "name": "Why they form and smell so strong",
      "char_file": "편도결석_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Tonsil stones form inside",
        "pockets on your tonsils",
        "called crypts",
        "",
        "Trapped food debris, dead cells,",
        "and bacteria calcify into",
        "a hard little lump",
        "",
        "Even a grain-sized stone",
        "can smell surprisingly strong",
        "when you press on it"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Frequent tonsillitis is a big driver",
      "char_file": "편도결석_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Repeated tonsil infections",
        "cause the crypts to widen",
        "and deepen over time",
        "",
        "That gives debris more room",
        "to collect and get trapped"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Treat infections and gargle with salt water",
      "char_file": "소금_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Treat tonsillitis promptly",
        "",
        "Gently rinse the back of",
        "your throat with warm salt water",
        "a couple times a day"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Dehydration and mouth breathing add up",
      "char_file": "입마름_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Saliva naturally rinses",
        "bacteria out of your throat",
        "",
        "Not drinking enough water,",
        "or breathing through your mouth",
        "while you sleep, slows that down"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Stay hydrated and fix mouth breathing",
      "char_file": "물컵_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Drink water throughout the day",
        "",
        "Address chronic mouth breathing,",
        "including nasal congestion",
        "or allergies that force it"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Leftover food debris feeds the crypts",
      "char_file": "칫솔_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Food particles left behind",
        "are the raw material",
        "tonsil stones are made of",
        "",
        "Brushing, flossing, and rinsing",
        "after meals cuts down",
        "what's available to get trapped"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Don't dig them out — here's what helps",
      "char_file": "손가락_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Resist digging them out",
        "with a finger or cotton swab —",
        "that can scrape the tissue",
        "",
        "If stones keep coming back,",
        "an ENT doctor can offer",
        "suction removal or cryptolysis"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "closing": {
    "headline": [
      [
        "Notice a small white speck",
        "that smells way worse than it looks?"
      ],
      [
        "Salt water gargles, hydration,",
        "and good oral hygiene keep them from coming back"
      ]
